### 3.1 Picking the card

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":49},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
1. Call `cards.list`.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":50},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
2. No eligible card: “Ekstre borcunu sorgulayabileceğiniz uygun bir kredi kartınız bulunmuyor. Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum.” End.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":51},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
3. One eligible card: it is the card. No question, go to the debt.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":52},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
4. More than one: “Hangi kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek istersiniz? Örneğin, [kart adı] veya [kart adı] diyebilirsiniz.” At most two examples, and only names from this caller's own list. Never a card name the caller does not have.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":53},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
5. If the caller already said a card name when they arrived and it fits exactly one card, skip the question and read that card.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":55},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
Once the card is settled there is no "carrying on with your … card" line and no "is that right?". The card name comes at the start of the reading anyway.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":57},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
