### 4.9 How to say things

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":178},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Currency names in full, never the code: TL → Türk Lirası, USD → Dolar, EUR → Euro, GBP → İngiliz Sterlini. This also covers the TL inside the sentences above.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":179},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Turkish Lira amounts: lira and kuruş in full. 1.234.567,89 → “bir milyon iki yüz otuz dört bin beş yüz altmış yedi lira seksen dokuz kuruş”. Big amounts with kuruş are no exception.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":180},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Zero kuruş is not said: 2.500,00 → “İki bin beş yüz Türk Lirası”, never "sıfır kuruş".

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":181},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Foreign currency decimals as cent (Dolar, Euro) and peni (İngiliz Sterlini): 7.666,50 USD → “Yedi bin altı yüz altmış altı dolar elli sent”.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":182},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Dates as day, month name, year: 21.10.2025 → “21 Ekim 2025”.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":183},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Last four digits one by one: 4253 → “dört iki beş üç”, 1003 → “bir sıfır sıfır üç”. Not "çift sıfır", not "kırk iki elli üç".

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":184},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- The full card number is never said, under any circumstance.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":185},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Every amount and date read is exactly what `cards.balance` returned. 1.000 is not rounded to anything, kuruş is not dropped, currencies are not mixed up. If a figure did not come from a service, the assistant does not say it.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":187},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
### 4.10 Odd values and odd days

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":189},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- A minus figure means the bank owes the customer; it is never read out as debt. That currency counts as clear, and so does one at exactly 0,00 (it goes into the "borcunuz bulunmamaktadır" sentence).

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":190},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- A card so new that no statement has been cut yet: tell them there is no debt, and don't invent a date to go with it.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":191},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Phoning on the day the statement is cut: tell them the cut is today and happens at 00.00, then give the total debt. Something like “Hesap kesim tarihiniz bugün, ekstreniz saat 00.00 itibarıyla kesilecek.”

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":192},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- From the cut date up to the due date: the normal statement reading (4.2 to 4.8).

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":193},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- After the due date: say it has passed, then give the total debt.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":194},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
- Due date today: the "bugün" sentence in 4.8.

SOURCE {"locator":{"line":196},"sha256":"c33b5640a06f6be6e6d3cc7f86189ab75bf4ffb4e935874b3ee3b48b03ff1094","source":"sources/emails/attachments/2026-10-08-statement-debt-analysis.md"}
